<title>GREECE: DELOS, EGNATIA LEAD GREEK GROWTH FUND RETURNS IN Q1.</title>
<headline>DELOS, EGNATIA LEAD GREEK GROWTH FUND RETURNS IN Q1.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delos Blue Chips and Egnatia</p>
<p>Bank's Olympia fund were leading Greece's 27 growth funds in the</p>
<p>first quarter of 1997 with returns of 43.9 and 41.3 percent</p>
<p>respectively, the association of institutional investors said.</p>
<p>But with the market returning 43.4 percent in the first</p>
<p>quarter the only outperformer was Delos Blue Chips as the other</p>
<p>26 funds including the index trackers were underperformers.</p>
<p>The benchmark general share index started the year at 954.54</p>
<p>and gained 414.28 points, 43.4 percent, to settle at 1,368.82 in</p>
<p>March 31.</p>
<p>Growth fund assets under management reached 112.2 billion</p>
<p>drachmas in end-March, up 32.8 percent since the beginning of</p>
<p>the year and 7.9 percent on February.</p>
<p>They made up 2.5 percent of the mutual fund industry's total</p>
<p>assets which rose to 4.82 trillion drachmas in the first quarter</p>
<p>-- an increase of 26 percent since the start of the year.</p>
